From b44dd1881482b73cb90d7dd74e10b5d2f000f165 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ebben Aries <exa@dscp.org>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 20:18:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(bar): stop forcing layer-shell commit on every
 onConfigure

942411d7 added an unconditional gtk_layer_try_force_commit() +
wl_display_flush() at the end of every Bar::onConfigure(), on top of
the existing forceLayerCommit() calls in setMode() and a one-shot idle
callback at construction. The intent was to work around gtk-layer-shell's
initial-configure wait timing out on a busy compositor and leaving the
bar invisible.

Rapid compositor-driven resizes on the same output (observed with
`kanshictl switch` reconfiguring a monitor) trigger several onConfigure
events in quick succession. Forcing a wl_surface.commit on every one,
independent of whether GTK has actually finished resizing/redrawing to
match the newly configured size, can submit a commit whose buffer
doesn't match the layer-surface's just-acked dimensions. wlroots'
layer-shell implementation treats that as a protocol violation and
kills the connection (Gdk-Message: Error 71 (Protocol error)
dispatching to Wayland display.), taking down the whole client with no
core dump.

Drop the forced commit from onConfigure. The construction-time idle
callback and the setMode() call already cover the invisible-bar
scenario 942411d7 targeted, without re-committing on every
compositor-driven resize.
---
 src/bar.cpp | 11 -----------
 1 file changed, 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/bar.cpp b/src/bar.cpp
index e15df373..0578dbc7 100644
--- a/src/bar.cpp
+++ b/src/bar.cpp
@@ -871,17 +871,6 @@ void waybar::Bar::onConfigure(GdkEventConfigure* ev) {
 #ifdef HAVE_BAR_BLUR
   updateBlurRegion();
 #endif
-
-  /*
-   * gtk-layer-shell waits for the compositor's initial configure while realizing the window. On a
-   * busy compositor (common during session startup) that wait can time out even though the initial
-   * configure arrives shortly afterwards. In that case GTK may not schedule the frame commit that
-   * presents the first layer-surface buffer, leaving an otherwise configured bar invisible. Force a
-   * commit after every configure so late initial configures, and later compositor-driven resizes,
-   * always result in a submitted surface state.
-   */
-  window.queue_draw();
-  forceLayerCommit();
 }
 
 void waybar::Bar::configureGlobalOffset(int width, int height) {
